; D8-v2 lowered-tree materialization: the emitted form's discriminant
; defaults via the *lowered* overlay.
;
; `sugar` lowers via test/identity-v1, which emits `sugar-normal` by
; convention. sugar declares no keys, so the hook emits `(sugar-
; normal)` with no kvpairs. sugar-normal is `:discriminant kind` with
; `:kind :default kick`. Without v2 the source overlay has no entry
; for the lowered `(sugar-normal)` node (its source NodeIndex is in
; the source-tree index space), so axis D fails to resolve the
; discriminant and emits `missing_discriminant_key at [sugar-normal]`.
; With v2 the lowered-tree overlay yields `kind = kick`, variant
; `kick` is selected, and the form validates silently.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name kind-tag
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [kick bass]))
  (form :name sugar :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/identity-v1 :produces [sugar-normal]))
  (form :name sugar-normal
    :discriminant kind
    (key :name kind :type kind-tag :default kick :optional true)
    (variant :when kick
      (key :name step :type number :optional true))
    (variant :when bass
      (key :name sequence :type any :optional true))))

(sugar)
